# The slow tests (17.3): tests that take most of the 200 s limit or more through
# dcfs, kept out of the normal set so that a shard fits its job, and run with a
# limit of 1500 s by the weekly set (xfstests_slow_<n>.sh; lists
# xfstests.slow.<fstype>.*). Their native times are in the reasons. Step 17.3
# attributed the extra time on a quiet host (docs/plan/notes/slowness-17.3.md): 80-98%
# daemon CPU (single-threaded SQLite queries and tri-state bookkeeping), not
# host load or disk wait. This file is the global set; xfstests.<fstype>.slow
# has the tests slow on one backing only.
